<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Amid France’s political 'fragmentation', 'a case needs to be made for participatory democracy’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b012ec19dfd955a607d93f38b0c711acce0ced3219bd1830d1bb91390edadb5f</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T08:01:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/amid-france-s-political-fragmentation-a-case-needs-to-be-made-for-participatory-democracy" /><summary type="html">Carys Garland is pleased to welcome Dr. Andrew Smith, Historian of Modern France and Lecturer in Liberal Arts at Queen Mary University of London. He argues that Marine Le Pen and the National Rally’s commanding position in early presidential polling should not be regarded as an inevitable far-right victory. They are benefiting from familiarity, unity and laser-focused messaging. More fundamentally, however, Smith sees the polling as a reflection of a French electorate shaped by anger, anxiety, economic insecurity and political fatigue. Rather than describing this landscape simply as one of growing “polarization,” he proposes the more revealing concept of “fragmentation.”</summary></entry><entry><title>Corruption ‘endemic’ in Trump administration: 'Checks and balances only in effect at lower courts'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cef389a7ef4ff6bf514f76c55b9b4a315c34e416758d56e9048688b9d66dd32</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:52:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260915-corruption-endemic-in-trump-administration-checks-and-balances-only-in-effect-at-lower-courts" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Andrew Weissmann, Author, Professor at NYU School of Law, and former General Counsel of the FBI. He argues that as political deception and deliberate falsehoods become normalized, and politically useful, it erodes any trust we have in our government and our institutions. Drawing on his book, "Liar’s Kingdom", Weissmann questions why political leaders are above the law in the United States, while ordinary citizens risk serious legal consequences for making intentionally false statements.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Lack of 'enforcement of EU laws': Consumer products contain 'illegal levels of restricted chemicals'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52167bfe11a783e467494241c52a5b348fd939a690762a49eee9d2e66d9ce6cb</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:28:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/lack-of-enforcement-of-eu-laws-consumer-products-contain-illegal-levels-of-restricted-chemicals" /><summary type="html">Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Hélène Duguy, Senior Environmental Lawyer at ClientEarth. PFAS pollution is widespread, these highly persistent chemicals have been detected in water and soil, food and consumer products, and even the human body. The risks are increasingly well documented, alternatives now exist for many uses, and there is an extensive regulatory framework that is in place. Duguy argues that the central problem is therefore not simply a lack of scientific knowledge or legislation, but rather weak enforcement, slow regulation and corporate resistance. And so hazardous chemicals remain in circulation even when restrictions exist.</summary></entry><entry><title>French labour strike reduces capacity at key Dunkirk gas terminal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:394aa16f60cdd0124f1454021aed6737558ee4839da1c864fa004a5f6ea8799f</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T07:24:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/france/20260915-french-labour-strike-reduces-capacity-key-dunkirk-gas-terminal" /><summary type="html">Industrial action ​was expected to reduce French electricity supply by up to 5 gigawatts on ⁠Tuesday as energy sector ⁠unions stage a 24-hour strike in protest over calls to curb ​employee benefits ‌such as access to cheaper power.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war exposes US munitions shortfall, industrial bottlenecks, Pentagon report says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a76f301c28ded0ca0e2d3d2614f905b182e2c0df65f535cac6e92b6f38218bc3</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T06:07:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-iran-war-exposes-us-munitions-shortfall-industrial-bottlenecks-pentagon-report-says" /><summary type="html">The US military faces shortages of key munitions due to the Iran war and industrial "bottlenecks" to rebuild stockpiles, a Pentagon watchdog warned in a report published on Monday, contradicting US President Donald Trump's assurances that ammunition supplies are "virtually unlimited".</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Mbappé, Yamal, Dembélé, Kane: Ballon d'Or campaign is in full swing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25308a35bd0d7efd8b6835eede04bccfb40c0f4011d48bc8e807718acfb8ead8</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T05:44:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260915-mbapp%C3%A9-yamal-demb%C3%A9l%C3%A9-kane-ballon-d-or-campaign-is-in-full-swing" /><summary type="html">With two weeks to go before voting closes for the Ballon d’Or, the leading contenders are campaigning.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Middle East live: Pentagon report says Iran war has led to munitions shortfall</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbbc55b1fb510d0f0a10527fda864e6055087820a01d802aaa965a0ef8896d26</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T05:28:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260915-middle-east-live-houthi-attacks-wound-13-civilians-in-southern-saudi-arabia--99d547e8fe8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260915-middle-east-live-houthi-attacks-wound-13-civilians-in-southern-saudi-arabia" /></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Iran rejects talks with US after 'mixed signals' from Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ecb3663b3817f52320be343a5017fea39b0b1b2a3fda312f6fbfa0ffef71b59</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T03:06:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260915-middle-east-live-houthi-attacks-wound-13-civilians-in-southern-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">Iran's security chief on Tuesday rejected talks with the United States, criticising the "mixed signals" from US President Donald Trump after he said he was open to resuming negotiations. The diplomatic deadlock comes as the US military is facing a shortfall in ammunition as a result of the war, according to a report by the Pentagon's inspector general. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela to join G20 energy talks in Texas at US invitation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c347f3f2f3228520152e7bfa4c4c42fefec33a7ba2afcac9e62542babc10b735</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T02:44:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-venezuela-to-join-g20-energy-meetings-in-texas-at-us-invitation" /><summary type="html">A Venezuelan delegation will join G20 energy talks in Houston this week as soaring oil prices and disruption from the Middle East war put global energy supplies under pressure. The meeting comes as the Trump administration deepens energy ties with Caracas and seeks to boost Venezuelan oil output.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine war live: NATO downs drone over Lithuania, Russian frigate fires flares at Danish helicopter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0efe55699133947b129b7de71c9dfc360b2ad8fc6927e43402d2759fae7b3a6</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T02:19:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260915-nato-fighter-jets-shoot-down-drone-over-lithuania-after-latest-incursion" /><summary type="html">NATO scrambled fighter jets overnight to ​shoot down a drone over Lithuania after the latest incursion on the alliance's eastern flank. In a separate incident, Denmark said a Russian warship fired two emergency flares at a Danish helicopter in the Baltic Sea, adding that the Russian ambassador had been summoned over the "reckless action". Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>US Supreme Court rejects Trump bid to restrict mail ballots as voting begins</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0dae94502d9d53901e997fd8580e3744e25ff8e1f483f017583b40a120954fcb</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T01:51:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260915-us-supreme-court-rejects-trump-bid-to-restrict-mail-ballots-as-voting-begins" /><summary type="html">The US Supreme Court on Monday rejected President Donald Trump’s bid to impose new restrictions on mail ballots ahead of November’s midterm elections. The ruling leaves states free to continue using existing voting procedures, after election officials warned the last-minute changes could disrupt ballot distribution.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Trump calls concerns over rogue AI a 'hoax' promoted by a ‘sick conspiracy’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e87a97028e756f191cad529060257b8c675706b00c92fd025a80bd978100810</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T01:05:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260915-trump-calls-concerns-over-rogue-ai-a-hoax-promoted-by-a-sick-conspiracy" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Monday rejected warnings about the risks of artificial intelligence, calling concerns over rogue AI part of a “sick conspiracy” as tech leaders urge greater safeguards. The clash comes as the rapidly advancing technology faces scrutiny over cybersecurity, jobs, data centres and its potential impact on national security.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's Dangote refinery launches biggest African IPO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:132a3f19ad423ae45a8f8ff399650757b9cb1d404112a8449605d221301fb05e</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T00:05:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/africa/20260915-nigeria-s-dangote-refinery-launches-biggest-african-ipo-for-retail-investors" /><summary type="html">Africa’s richest man Aliko Dangote on Monday launched an IPO for his $19 billion Nigerian oil refinery, seeking $1.6 billion from retail investors across the continent. The offering values Africa’s largest refinery at about $49 billion and has drawn both strong investor interest and concerns over its high valuation.</summary><category term="Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky says Ukraine ready to de-escalate if Russia halts strikes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5239b62c0a9452e3dad8c7f936bd88468f8ade1d2a200eefce73dd28af74178c</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T22:57:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260914-zelensky-says-ukraine-ready-to-de-escalate-if-russia-halts-strikes" /><summary type="html">Ukraine is ready to halt attacks on Russian energy infrastructure if Moscow does the same, President Volodymyr Zelensky said Monday, after US President Donald Trump announced an apparent agreement between the two sides. Kyiv also warned that intensifying Russian strikes on Ukraine’s rail network are worsening each week.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Rapper Macklemore dropped from Ed Sheeran's US tour after pro-Palestinian remarks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3de5fa25d10774fb30991ca6b64421b4515b7e6d4343f999852b53683be42183</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T22:20:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-macklemore-dropped-from-ed-sheeran-us-tour-after-pro-palestinian-remarks" /><summary type="html">American rapper Macklemore announced Monday that he was dropped from British singer Ed Sheeran’s US stadium tour after saying "Free Palestine" during a September 4 concert in New Jersey. The Grammy winner’s removal follows pressure from venue owners, including New England Patriots owner Robert Kraft, over his criticism of Israel’s actions in Gaza.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>US Space Force confirms weapons deployed in space for first time</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d6b08d8a5557f5799c018f51a0e7e54b9971afcbbd686cc1c9ebc4cd6615b2ec</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260914-us-space-force-confirms-weapons-deployed-in-space-for-first-time" /><summary type="html">The US Space Force on Monday confirmed for the first time that Washington has weapons deployed in orbit, as the United States, China and Russia expand their military capabilities in space. The disclosure highlights a growing focus on controlling the space domain and protecting satellites vital to military communications, surveillance and navigation.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Bob Mackie, fashion designer for the stars, dies at 87</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c11d9e5d77d62cb45cd4c0e39f7d4f22538bef40e99d19bdd4c8141c5426936</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:40:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/bob-mackie-fashion-designer-for-the-stars-dies-at-87" /><summary type="html">⁠Hollywood designer ⁠Bob Mackie, ​known for making stars such as Cher and ​Elton John sparkle, died on Monday at 87, according to a post on his official Instagram account. His career ​spanned ‌five decades and included ⁠designing a Barbie doll clothes collection. FRANCE 24's Camille Knight has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rights group accuses Israel of dismantling 'Palestinian existence' in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ab6e944dbef5e581a97e4ad892ceba7e611939edd6be0e964da1b7f9941cc08</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:26:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/rights-group-accuses-israel-of-dismantling-palestinian-existence-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">Israeli rights group B'Tselem said Monday that Israeli actions in the occupied West Bank form part of a greater project designed to make it impossible for Palestinians to exist together as a people. In a report titled "The Elimination Project", the group alleged five connected Israeli tactics and policies in the West Bank: "violence, ethnic cleansing, movement restrictions, economic strangulation, social and political destruction". FRANCE 24's Selina Sykes reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fact-checking videos claiming to show Houthi rebel attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dbdd743d6098dfb7484df34d8a3d4049cda1d4f660b8b63c02bea8aa7720bd20</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:10:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fact-checking-videos-claiming-to-show-houthi-rebel-attacks-1" /><summary type="html">A video claiming to show Houthi rebels ambushing Saudi-backed mercenaries has racked up major views on X. But the FRANCE 24 Observers found it is actually footage of 2024 Houthi military drills. The clip was edited with football commentary and blurred flags, which originally show Israel, the UK and US, not Saudi Arabia. Other viral videos falsely linked to Houthi attacks on a Saudi Aramco refinery were also traced to unrelated fires in Texas and Russia. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'The very existence of LGBTQI people is seen as obscene', Turkish activist says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c35464ac2878781ecb688a092984a298601a51d096c24133af034d21f2fa499</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T21:02:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260914-the-very-existence-of-lgbtqi-people-is-seen-as-obscene-turkish-activist-says" /><summary type="html">Turkish police on Sunday swooped on gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists, arresting at least 60 people in raids authorities said were aimed at boosting traditional family values, officials and activists said. Turkey's LGBTQ community has frequently been targeted by the government, with President Recep Tayyip Erdogan lashing it as a "deviant movement" of "perverts" responsible for the falling birth rate. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Yildiz Tar, Editor-in-Chief of KaosGL.org.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Dozens arrested in major anti-LGBTQ raids in Turkey</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e9b55fd762cf859d5719b65efd7c8d0c7aa3d3033f7fcb0131243ff25dd2f9a</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T20:57:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/dozens-arrested-in-major-anti-lgbtq-raids-in-turkey" /><summary type="html">Turkish police on Sunday swooped on gay bars and the homes of LGBTQ activists, arresting at least 60 people in raids authorities said were aimed at boosting traditional family values, officials and activists said. Turkey's LGBTQ community has frequently been targeted by the government, with President Recep Tayyip Erdogan lashing it as a "deviant movement" of "perverts" responsible for the falling birth rate. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis speaks with Yildiz Tar, Editor-in-Chief of KaosGL.org.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's Dangote refinery kicks off blockbuster IPO</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9f65b71708dfbfcafdacb610ad2368056fc34f2ac9b7aa56e69cc1727d10ffa</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T20:46:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260914-nigeria-s-dangote-refinery-kicks-off-blockbuster-ipo" /><summary type="html">Nigerian billionaire Aliko Dangote launched the biggest-ever share sale on the African continent, listing 4.1 billion shares in his Lagos refinery on the stock exchange.  He framed it as a "people's IPO" to give all Nigerians a chance to share the plant's wealth potentials. Trading is expected to start in November. Meanwhile, global oil prices continued to advance as attacks by Yemen's Houthi rebels forced Saudi Arabia to shut down its East-West oil pipeline.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Nigerian oil refinery Dangote aims to raise 1.6 billion dollars</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:682d7675dd5e92444ca5f2178dbbb8639343e10827d86efc737ee4c4ad39b3af</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T20:31:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/nigerian-oil-refinery-dangote-aims-to-raise-1-6-billion-dollars" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Nigeria's Dangote refinery opens itself to public ownership with plans to raise 1.6 billion dollars from retail investors across the continent. Also, President Felix Tshisekedi calls on the National Service to clean up the streets of Kinshasa. And with a month and a half to go until the Youth Olympic Games begin, the Olympic flame begins its tour of Senegal, the tournament's host country.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey police disperse pro-LGBTQ protesters with tear gas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7845676a90d406ac2ec661b4838c846021ee278c88b8de9a71f3e156757d8b08</id><updated>2026-09-15T13:41:15Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T19:54:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="http://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260914-turkey-police-disperse-pro-lgbtq-protesters-with-tear-gas" /><summary type="html">Turkish police fired tear gas at pro-LGBTQ demonstrators in the western city of Izmir on Monday, as activists protested a nationwide crackdown that saw dozens arrested over the weekend in a campaign authorities described as defending traditional family values.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry></feed>
